<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22415" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incōgĭtātus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		2. in-cogito. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>unconsidered</i>, <i>unstudied</i> (postAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ben. 6, 23 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alacritas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Ep. 57</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incogitata dicere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Flor. p. 364</span></i>
			 (de Deo. Soc. p. 102 Hild.).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>thoughtless</i>, <i>inconsiderate</i> (ante- and postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Bacch. 4, 3, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne incogitati dicere cogerentur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lampr. Alex. Sev. 16</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
